# What do people normally do to keep fit and healthy in your country?
In my country, many people try to stay fit by doing simple and accessible activities. For example, a lot of people go jogging or walking in parks, especially in the early morning or evening. Others prefer going to the gym or joining fitness classes like yoga or aerobics. In addition, playing sports such as badminton or football is also quite popular, especially among young people. Recently, more people have started paying attention to their diet as well, choosing healthier food options. Overall, people are becoming more health-conscious than before.

# How do children and old people keep fit and healthy?
I think children and older people stay healthy in different ways. Children usually keep fit through physical activities like playing sports, running, or participating in outdoor games, often at school or with friends. These activities help them stay active without feeling like they are exercising.

On the other hand, older people tend to prefer lighter forms of exercise, such as walking, yoga, or doing gentle stretching. They also pay more attention to their diet and regular health check-ups. Overall, both groups stay healthy, but their approaches depend on their age and physical condition.
